      title: "ArgentoFX API"
      version: "1.0.0"
      tagline: "Live quotations for the US dollar and other foreign currencies in Argentina"
      homepage: "https://fastapiproject-1-eziw.onrender.com"
      docs_url: "https://fastapiproject-1-eziw.onrender.com/docs"
      about_md: `ArgentoFX is a small REST API that exposes live foreign-currency quotations for Argentina, with a focus on the various parallel "dollar" rates (blue, oficial, etc.) that circulate alongside the official peso exchange rate. The service is hosted on Render at [fastapiproject-1-eziw.onrender.com](https://fastapiproject-1-eziw.onrender.com) and is catalogued on [Free Public APIs](https://freepublicapis.com/argentofx-api).

What you get from the API:

- Endpoints for individual dollar quotes (for example \`GET /blue\` for the blue-dollar rate).
- Quotations for other foreign currencies traded in Argentina.
- A root endpoint that serves as the entry point to the service.

Interactive OpenAPI documentation is available at \`/docs\`. The upstream catalogue notes that CORS is disabled and that the deployment has been intermittently unreachable, so callers should expect to handle errors and downtime.`
      entity_desc: {
        currency: "Foreign-currency quotations available in Argentina beyond the US dollar."
        dollar_quote: "US dollar quotations against the Argentine peso, including parallel rates such as the blue dollar (for example `GET /blue`)."
        get_root: "The service root endpoint (`GET /`), typically used as a health or welcome response."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
